To fix this issue, ensure the Cipher instance and parameters comply with all defined constraints. Here are key guidelines based on the CrySL rule:<br><br><b>Key-Algorithm Matching:</b><ul><li>If <code>key</code> is a <code>SecretKey</code>, then <code>transformation</code> must use one of:<br><code>{AES, PBEWithHmacSHAxxxAndAES_xxx}</code></li><li>If using <code>PublicKey</code>, <code>PrivateKey</code>, or <code>Certificate</code> and <code>encmode</code> in <code>{3, 4}</code>, then <code>transformation</code> must be <code>RSA</code></li></ul><br><b>Algorithm, Mode, and Padding Combinations:</b><ul><li><code>AES</code> must use one of these modes: <code>{GCM, CTR, CTS, CFB, OFB}</code> and <b>must use</b> <code>NoPadding</code></li><li><code>RSA</code>:<ul><li><code>mode == ""</code> → <code>pad == ""</code></li><li><code>mode == "ECB"</code> → <code>pad</code> must be one of: <code>NoPadding, PKCS1Padding, OAEPWithSHA-xxxAndMGF1Padding</code></li></ul></li><li><code>PBEWithHmacSHAxxxAndAES_xxx</code> must use <code>PKCS5Padding</code></li></ul><br><b>IV Requirements:</b><ul><li>If mode is <code>{CTR, CTS, CFB, OFB}</code> and <code>encmode == 1</code>, then <code>getIV()</code> must be called</li><li>If <code>encmode != 1</code>, then <code>init()</code> must not use IV-related overloads</li></ul><br><b>AAD Restrictions:</b><ul><li>Only allowed when <code>mode == GCM</code></li><li>Disallowed in modes: <code>CTR, CTS, CFB, ECB, OFB</code></li></ul><br><b>Offset/Length Constraints:</b><ul><li><code>prePlainTextOffset >= 0</code>, <code>prePlainTextLen > 0</code>, and <code>prePlainText.length >= prePlainTextOffset + prePlainTextLen</code></li><li><code>plainTextOffset >= 0</code>, <code>plainTextLen > 0</code>, and <code>plainText.length >= plainTextOffset + plainTextLen</code></li><li><code>preCipherTextOffset >= 0</code> and <code>preCipherText.length >= preCipherTextOffset</code></li><li><code>cipherTextOffset >= 0</code> and <code>cipherText.length >= cipherTextOffset</code></li></ul><br> <b>Mode setting must be valid:</b><ul><li><code>encmode</code> must be one of: <code>{1, 2, 3, 4}</code></li></ul><br><b>Example Fix:</b><br><pre><code>import javax.crypto.Cipher;
import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;

public class AESExample {
 public byte[] encrypt(byte[] plainText) throws Exception {
 KeyGenerator keyGen = KeyGenerator.getInstance("AES");
 keyGen.init(256);
 SecretKey key = keyGen.generateKey();

 Cipher cipher = Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding");
 cipher.init(Cipher.ENCRYPT_MODE, key);
        return cipher.doFinal(plainText);
}
}</code></pre><br><b>Avoid:</b><ul><li>Using <code>RSA</code> with <code>CTR</code> or <code>GCM</code></li><li>Setting incorrect <code>offset</code> and <code>length</code> values on byte arrays</li><li>Calling <code>updateAAD()</code> outside of <code>GCM</code> mode</li><li>Using mismatched <code>Key</code> types and algorithms</li></ul>

